1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,350
A tomato.

2
00:00:01,101 --> 00:00:02,001
A brinjal.

3
00:00:01,792 --> 00:00:02,692
A potato.

4
00:00:02,843 --> 00:00:06,663
One is red, one is purple,
and one grows under the soil.

5
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:09,636
Yet all three come from
the same plant family.

6
00:00:10,086 --> 00:00:11,599
Aarav loves short codes.

7
00:00:11,599 --> 00:00:14,939
He is aiming for JEE, and
he knows water is H two O.

8
00:00:14,939 --> 00:00:18,726
He asked: can a whole flower be
written in one line like that?

9
00:00:19,076 --> 00:00:19,976
It can.

10
00:00:19,693 --> 00:00:23,305
Botanists write a floral formula,
a one line code for a flower.

11
00:00:23,805 --> 00:00:28,345
By the end, you will read and write a
floral formula, and use it to describe

12
00:00:28,345 --> 00:00:30,239
the potato family, Solanaceae.

13
00:00:30,889 --> 00:00:34,099
First, how does a botanist
describe a flowering plant?

14
00:00:34,449 --> 00:00:35,687
In a fixed order.

15
00:00:35,687 --> 00:00:38,679
First its habit and its
roots, stem and leaves.

16
00:00:38,679 --> 00:00:40,767
Then its flowers and their parts.

17
00:00:41,217 --> 00:00:46,285
The flower is written as a floral
formula, and drawn as a floral diagram.

18
00:00:46,735 --> 00:00:51,651
In a floral diagram, a dot on top shows
the mother axis, the stem the flower

19
00:00:51,651 --> 00:00:52,553
grows from.

20
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:57,401
Then come the rings, from the calyx
outside to the gynoecium in the centre.

21
00:00:58,051 --> 00:00:58,980
Now, the code.

22
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,966
Each part of the flower gets a symbol.

23
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:05,312
Br means the flower has a
bract, a small leaf at its base.

24
00:01:05,312 --> 00:01:09,864
A circle with a cross means actinomorphic,
a flower you can cut into two

25
00:01:09,864 --> 00:01:13,067
equal halves through any
plane through its centre.

26
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:16,677
A percent sign means zygomorphic,
only one plane works.

27
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:19,469
K is the calyx, the whorl of sepals.

28
00:01:19,469 --> 00:01:21,849
C is the corolla, the whorl of petals.

29
00:01:21,849 --> 00:01:25,257
P is the perianth, used when
sepals and petals look alike.

30
00:01:25,757 --> 00:01:27,909
A is the androecium, the stamens.

31
00:01:27,909 --> 00:01:30,016
G is the gynoecium, the carpels.

32
00:01:30,016 --> 00:01:33,025
A line under the G number
means a superior ovary.

33
00:01:33,025 --> 00:01:35,515
A line above it means an inferior ovary.

34
00:01:36,015 --> 00:01:39,788
A number in brackets means the
parts are fused, joined together.

35
00:01:39,788 --> 00:01:44,160
A line drawn above two symbols means
adhesion, one whorl joined to another.

36
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:49,414
Now let's decode one real formula,
for the potato family, and build its

37
00:01:49,414 --> 00:01:51,395
floral diagram ring by ring.

38
00:01:51,745 --> 00:01:52,645
Step one.

39
00:01:52,524 --> 00:01:55,507
A circle with a cross,
and the bisexual sign.

40
00:01:55,507 --> 00:01:59,459
The flower is actinomorphic, and
has both stamens and a pistil.

41
00:02:00,209 --> 00:02:01,109
Step two.

42
00:02:00,841 --> 00:02:01,952
K five in brackets.

43
00:02:01,952 --> 00:02:03,131
Five sepals, joined.

44
00:02:03,131 --> 00:02:06,146
They stay on, even on the
fruit, so they are persistent.

45
00:02:06,146 --> 00:02:08,058
Look at the green cap on a brinjal.

46
00:02:08,808 --> 00:02:09,708
Step three.

47
00:02:09,601 --> 00:02:10,842
C five in brackets.

48
00:02:10,842 --> 00:02:12,427
Five petals, also joined.

49
00:02:13,177 --> 00:02:14,077
Step four.

50
00:02:13,872 --> 00:02:16,019
A five, with a line joining it to C.

51
00:02:16,019 --> 00:02:17,942
Five stamens, fixed on the petals.

52
00:02:17,942 --> 00:02:19,123
They are epipetalous.

53
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:20,773
Step five.

54
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:22,918
G two in brackets, with a line below.

55
00:02:22,918 --> 00:02:26,049
Two fused carpels in a
superior ovary, with two rooms.

56
00:02:26,049 --> 00:02:28,245
A swollen placenta carries many ovules.

57
00:02:28,245 --> 00:02:29,824
That is axile placentation.

58
00:02:30,574 --> 00:02:32,208
Now meet the family itself.

59
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:34,410
Solanaceae is called the potato family.

60
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:38,571
The plants are mostly herbs
and shrubs, rarely small trees.

61
00:02:38,571 --> 00:02:42,343
The leaves are simple and
alternate, with a net of veins.

62
00:02:42,843 --> 00:02:45,667
In potato, a stem grows under the soil.

63
00:02:45,667 --> 00:02:48,663
The potato we eat is a stem, not a root.

64
00:02:49,163 --> 00:02:53,231
The fruits are berries or capsules, with
many seeds that keep their endosperm.

65
00:02:53,731 --> 00:02:55,148
This family feeds us.

66
00:02:55,148 --> 00:02:57,457
Tomato, brinjal and potato are food.

67
00:02:57,457 --> 00:02:58,736
Chilli is a spice.

68
00:02:58,736 --> 00:03:03,014
Belladonna and ashwagandha give medicine,
tobacco is fumigatory, and petunia

69
00:03:03,014 --> 00:03:04,670
is grown for its flowers.

70
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,078
Two code marks get mixed up.

71
00:03:07,078 --> 00:03:10,986
Brackets show fusion, parts of the
same whorl joined, like five sepals

72
00:03:10,986 --> 00:03:11,886
in one cup.

73
00:03:12,593 --> 00:03:16,828
A line drawn above two symbols shows
adhesion, parts of different whorls

74
00:03:16,828 --> 00:03:19,253
joined, like stamens fixed on petals.

75
00:03:20,003 --> 00:03:24,483
A line under the G number means a
superior ovary, sitting above the other

76
00:03:24,483 --> 00:03:26,066
parts, as in brinjal.

77
00:03:26,066 --> 00:03:29,397
A line above means an
inferior ovary, as in guava.

78
00:03:30,147 --> 00:03:31,047
Your turn.

79
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:35,025
A formula shows C five in brackets,
and a line joining C to A.

80
00:03:35,025 --> 00:03:36,718
Which mark shows adhesion?

81
00:03:36,718 --> 00:03:37,928
Pause and decide.

82
00:03:41,128 --> 00:03:42,028
The line!

83
00:03:41,817 --> 00:03:44,573
It joins stamens to petals,
two different whorls.

84
00:03:44,573 --> 00:03:46,900
The brackets show fusion inside one whorl.

85
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:48,450
Remember this.

86
00:03:48,435 --> 00:03:50,601
Brackets mean joined in the same whorl.

87
00:03:50,601 --> 00:03:52,685
A line means joined to another whorl.

88
00:03:53,285 --> 00:03:54,733
Now, a worked example.

89
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:58,614
Let's write the formula of a makoi
flower, Solanum nigrum, from what we

90
00:03:58,614 --> 00:03:59,514
see.

91
00:03:59,401 --> 00:04:03,232
The flower looks the same all
round, and has both sexes.

92
00:04:03,232 --> 00:04:06,229
Circle with a cross,
and the bisexual sign.

93
00:04:06,679 --> 00:04:07,688
Five sepals, joined.

94
00:04:07,688 --> 00:04:08,638
K five in brackets.

95
00:04:09,088 --> 00:04:10,212
Five petals, joined.

96
00:04:10,212 --> 00:04:11,270
C five in brackets.

97
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,296
Five stamens on the petals.

98
00:04:13,296 --> 00:04:14,971
A five, with a line to C.

99
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:17,917
Two fused carpels, and
the ovary is superior.

100
00:04:17,917 --> 00:04:20,088
G two in brackets, with a line below.

101
00:04:20,538 --> 00:04:23,200
Put it together, and one line
describes the whole flower.

102
00:04:23,850 --> 00:04:25,311
Now, the exam trap.

103
00:04:25,661 --> 00:04:28,929
Many students think a line drawn
above the symbols means fusion.

104
00:04:29,329 --> 00:04:31,338
But fusion is shown by brackets.

105
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:35,493
The line above shows adhesion, one
whorl joined to another, like stamens

106
00:04:35,493 --> 00:04:36,393
on petals.

107
00:04:36,934 --> 00:04:38,279
Where is this asked?

108
00:04:38,279 --> 00:04:42,370
As formula reading: what a floral
formula tells you, or which family a

109
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:43,796
description belongs to.

110
00:04:44,396 --> 00:04:45,405
Exam level now.

111
00:04:45,405 --> 00:04:47,808
Which statement about
Solanaceae is correct?

112
00:04:47,808 --> 00:04:48,859
Pause and solve.

113
00:04:54,259 --> 00:04:55,524
The answer is A.

114
00:04:56,024 --> 00:04:59,839
The line joining A to C shows
epipetalous stamens, and the line below G

115
00:04:59,839 --> 00:05:01,216
shows a superior ovary.

116
00:05:01,716 --> 00:05:05,691
The ovary has two rooms with axile
placentation, and the five sepals are

117
00:05:05,691 --> 00:05:07,034
joined and persistent.

118
00:05:07,634 --> 00:05:09,175
Here is your recap.

119
00:05:09,175 --> 00:05:10,759
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:13,959 --> 00:05:16,145
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

121
00:05:16,545 --> 00:05:17,445
One.

122
00:05:17,003 --> 00:05:20,435
What does a circle with a
cross mean in a floral formula?

123
00:05:21,335 --> 00:05:22,235
Two.

124
00:05:21,781 --> 00:05:24,255
How is adhesion shown in a floral formula?

125
00:05:25,155 --> 00:05:26,055
Three.

126
00:05:25,581 --> 00:05:27,370
Write the floral formula of Solanaceae.

127
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:31,286
Next time: why does a pea
flower look like a butterfly?

128
00:05:31,286 --> 00:05:33,787
We find out in the families
Fabaceae and Liliaceae.
